{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix landed locally (NOT pushed) — ticket deliberately left OPEN pending live validation\n\nCommit `443609b8989de8391b44a813ca91b6b2a4a30a47` on worktree branch `d43e-bedrock-extra`\n(`/Users/joeoakhart/d43e-bedrock-extra`), signed off, trailer verified\n(`rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` -> OK).\n\n### What changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` | `uv sync … --extra agents --extra mcp` -> `… --extra bedrock` (the root cause) |\n| `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` | `mcp` service gains `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` + `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` = `us-east-1` |\n| `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` | `mcp_run_new` gains the same two `-e` flags (the path a real deploy takes) |\n| `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` | +3 guards (coupling + two parity), 153 lines |\n\n`[agents]` and `[bedrock]` are kept SEPARATE rather than flattened. Checked the history first:\nthe split is deliberate (ticket sporadic-bratty-porcupine — \"boto3 stays out of the default\ninstall\"), and `[agents]` is what every PyPI consumer of `nava-rebar` installs, so folding\nboto3 in would tax every non-Bedrock adopter to fix one deployment. `Dockerfile.reviewbot` had\nalready made exactly this declaration on 2026-08-03, three weeks before `Dockerfile.mcp` was\nauthored — which is also why the attribution lands on fd4a-4e91-f179-4932 rather than on the\nBedrock cutover.\n\n### RED -> GREEN -> mutation\n\n- **RED** (before fix): all three new tests fail. The coupling guard's message names the gap\n  precisely — \"Dockerfile.mcp installs extras ['agents', 'mcp'], which cannot serve every\n  provider configured in rebar.toml (['anthropic', 'bedrock']): missing extra(s) ['bedrock']\".\n- **GREEN** (after fix): `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` 30 passed.\n- **Mutation** (sandboxed under `sandbox-exec`, writes denied outside the worktree): each of\n  the three changes re-removed individually returns exactly its own test to RED, and restoring\n  returns all 30 to green.\n- **Coupling mutation**: re-pointing `rebar.toml` at `openai:gpt-4o` with the Dockerfile\n  UNTOUCHED also fails the guard — so it is a genuine config<->image coupling check, not a\n  string match on the `uv sync` line.\n- **Dependency-level replication of the original report**: a venv built with the image's OLD\n  extras `[agents,mcp]` raises the reported error verbatim; one built with the NEW extras\n  `[agents,mcp,bedrock]` returns `BUILT OK: BedrockProvider`.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` exit 0 (incl. the shrink-only complexity ratchet: `new=0 increased=0`),\n`make typecheck` exit 0 (678 files), `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` 4 passed (no\n`src/rebar` file touched, so the 800-LOC CI gate is unaffected), and the FULL unit suite\n**14009 passed, 51 skipped** — no regressions.\n\n`rebar review-plan` on this ticket: **PASS, signed** (0 blocking, 1 advisory, 1 coaching;\n`llm_ran: true`, `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`, attested at\n`97b003c4cd0e0d448595d87e994e5999fedee7f5`). Run through the LOCAL repo `.venv` CLI — which is\nthe whole point of this bug: the same op through the deployed MCP server still cannot run.\n\n### Provider audit against the operator directive (\"Bedrock for ALL\")\n\n- Every gate YAML binds model **CLASSES**, not bare ids (`plan-review.yaml`, `code-review.yaml`),\n  and `rebar.toml`'s class table points all three at Bedrock. Good.\n- **Every built-in default is direct-Anthropic**: `DEFAULT_MODEL = \"claude-opus-4-8\"`\n  (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:65`), `VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"` (`:71`),\n  `TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL = \"claude-haiku-4-5\"` (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:45`), and any\n  bare `claude*` infers `anthropic` (`config.py:179-187`). These only fire if the config is not\n  discovered — and `_read_llm_file_table` SWALLOWS a `ConfigError` and degrades to `{}`\n  (`config.py:369-372`), so an unreadable `rebar.toml` in the container would silently serve\n  every class from direct Anthropic rather than failing closed. Recorded as residual risk below.\n- **`rebar.toml:209-210` gives `frontier` and `standard` direct-`anthropic:` fallbacks**, and\n  `should_fall_back` (`model_classes.py:366-393`) uses them on availability errors. The\n  container also receives a real `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from `.env`\n  (`infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh:210`), so that arm is LIVE. **NOT changed** — `rebar.toml:181-187`\n  records an explicit operator decision (2026-08-07) that this arm is approved, and the table is\n  repo-wide, so editing it would change local dev and CI too. **Operator decision required** if\n  the deployed server is to be Bedrock-only.\n- Two non-class residual paths ride the scalar `cfg.model`: `spec_scan.py:127` and\n  `overlap/digest_sidecar.py:151-157`. `rebar.toml:198` sets that scalar to Bedrock, so they\n  are correct today, but they are the paths that would fall to `DEFAULT_MODEL` if config\n  discovery failed.\n\n### Credentials / region (verified read-only against AWS, not assumed)\n\nInstance `i-00880b2c7f13527c5` is in **us-east-1**, profile `rebar-gerrit-instance-profile` ->\nrole `rebar-gerrit-instance-role`, which carries inline policy `rebar-gerrit-bedrock-converse`\nallowing `bedrock:InvokeModel` + `InvokeModelWithResponseStream` on\n`arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-*` and\n`arn:aws:bedrock:*:896586841071:inference-profile/*.anthropic.claude-*`. **Credentials and\npermissions are already in place**; no operator action needed there. Region was the gap and is\nnow set explicitly in both deploy paths.\n\n### Sibling sweep (Step 7)\n\n- **Axis 1 (construct).** `Dockerfile.reviewbot` already declares `--extra bedrock` — correct.\n  `Dockerfile.opcert:39` does **not**, yet `src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:68-76` dispatches\n  the real `review_plan`/`verify_completion`. It is not currently broken only because\n  `reviewbot = [..., \"boto3\"]` satisfies the provider INCIDENTALLY — precisely the latent\n  accident `Dockerfile.reviewbot`'s own comment warns about. **Filed as\n  atrophied-unbeatable-hermitcrab (e46b-9ca3-d1b3-4dd4)**, linked `discovered_from` this bug,\n  with file impact set. Not fixed in scope: it is a different service, not currently failing,\n  and the operator directive was scoped to the MCP instance.\n- **Axis 2 (parity).** Surfaces for this operation are Dockerfile / compose service /\n  autodeploy `docker run`. All three are now covered: the extra in the Dockerfile, and region\n  in BOTH compose and `mcp_run_new` (compose-only would never have reached a deployed\n  container). `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml` is the CI matrix arm, N/A here.\n\n### Residual risk (observed, dispositioned)\n\n- **ACCEPTED / operator call:** the direct-Anthropic fallback arm above.\n- **ACCEPTED, worth a ticket if you want it:** there is **no startup preflight** for the\n  configured provider. `_capabilities.py:100-107` defines a `bedrock_provider` capability with\n  an ERROR posture, but neither `require_capability` nor `is_available` is called anywhere in\n  `src/` for it — the only `guard_import` call site in the tree is\n  `metrics/analyzers/lizard_complexity.py:30`. So a misconfigured container starts CLEAN and\n  fails only at first gate invocation, which is exactly why this bug reached production\n  silently. A boot-time capability check would have failed the container closed instead.\n- **ACCEPTED:** `_read_llm_file_table` swallowing `ConfigError` into `{}` (`config.py:369-372`)\n  means an unreadable config degrades to direct-Anthropic defaults rather than failing closed.\n\n### Why this ticket is NOT being closed\n\nAcceptance criterion 2 as originally written is a **live-validation** criterion: \"`review_plan`\nvia the MCP server … returns `coverage.llm_ran = true` … and `signature.signed = true` —\nchecked by re-running the tool and inspecting the returned JSON.\" That can only be observed\nagainst the **deployed** server, which requires the operator to land this change and redeploy.\nNothing in this session can honestly tick it, so the ticket stays `in_progress`.\n\n**Operator next steps:** land `443609b8989d` through Gerrit, redeploy the mcp service, then\nre-run `review_plan` through the MCP server and confirm `llm_ran: true` / `signed: true`. Note\nthe criterion's own suggested probe (`find_spec('pydantic_ai.models.bedrock')`) is a WEAK\noracle and would have passed on the broken container — measured, that module ships with\n`pydantic-ai-slim` unconditionally and is truthy while `boto3` is absent. Probe `boto3`, or\nimport the provider."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787869750054201001,"uuid":"327d3bb9-8432-43f1-879b-58830fb1db20"}